# Mash's global excludes, read by git inside Mash panes.
#
# Mash pins XDG_CONFIG_HOME to ~/.mash/config, so git's default global excludes
# file resolves here -- ~/.mash/config/git/ignore -- without any core.excludesFile
# entry. It applies to every repository a pane works in.
#
# .mash/ holds the working directories the Mash Programming Skills write
# (brainstorms, plans, solutions, insights, qa, parallel, ...). They are working
# state, not project source, so they stay out of every repository. A directory
# pattern matches at any depth, so a nested repo is covered too.
#
# Seeded once by the launcher; this file is yours after that. The host's own
# global gitignore (~/.gitignore-global) is deliberately not touched: Mash keeps
# its git configuration separate from the account's.
.mash/
